**Standard error (the “null‑hypothesis” standard deviation)**  

\[
SE = \frac{s}{\sqrt{n}}
    = \frac{1.4}{\sqrt{40}}
    \approx \frac{1.4}{6.3249}
    \approx 0.22
\]

So the standard deviation of the sampling distribution of the mean under the null hypothesis \(H_0:\mu=98.6\) is roughly **0.22**.
